1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Every P2P crypto deal has a trust paradox: pay upfront and risk getting scammed, deliver work first and risk getting ghosted, or use centralized escrow and accept custody risk.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:19,500
Meet SafeDeal — non-custodial P2P escrow on Avalanche, where smart contracts hold the funds, RFC 8785 locks the terms, and no admin can ever touch your AVAX.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Flow 1: Cooperative Trade. The seller drafts deal terms and SafeDeal hashes them deterministically with RFC 8785 in both TypeScript and Rust, anchoring termsHash on Avalanche Fuji.

4
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:43,000
The buyer funds the vault, the seller marks delivery, and the buyer approves and releases payment on-chain.

5
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:57,000
Notice SafeDeal uses Pull-Payment withdraw instead of inline pushes, crediting claimable balances to eliminate reentrancy and reverting-recipient denial-of-service attacks.

6
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:09,000
The seller simply withdraws their settled AVAX directly from the contract.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:22,500
Flow 2: Open-Buyer and Refund Protection. Leave the buyer address blank to create a shareable payment link, and the first wallet to fund locks in as the buyer.

8
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:36,500
If the seller misses the delivery deadline or issues a voluntary refund, the buyer reclaims one hundred percent of their AVAX directly on-chain without needing admin permission.

9
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Flow 3: Dispute and 2-of-3 Consensus. When a deal goes wrong, participants upload private evidence validated by binary magic-bytes and gated by Sign-In with Ethereum.

10
00:01:51,500 --> 00:02:02,000
Outsiders receive a strict 403 error, ensuring private dispute files stay visible only to the buyer, seller, and arbiter.

11
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:16,500
Unlike traditional escrows where a single arbiter has god-mode, SafeDeal requires 2-of-3 matching votes across Buyer, Seller, and Arbiter to settle.

12
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:32,000
And if everyone ghosts, a 14-day timeout fallback unlocks a deterministic 50/50 split so funds are never trapped.

13
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:48,000
Built with Solidity and Foundry invariant fuzzing, a Clean Architecture Rust backend on Railway, and a reload-safe React UI live on Avalanche Fuji.

14
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:58,000
Try SafeDeal today at avalanche-9b099.web.app.
